{"vid":"SamV6zpRNgg","source":"SamV6zpRNgg.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.2,"txt":"I'm going to explain all about instrumentation calibration and why is so vital in industry."},{"t":6.1,"txt":"Let us start with an overview of what calibration is and why it is needed, I will then discuss the"},{"t":11.4,"txt":"calibration process and talk about calibration frequency. As we learnt in the transmitter lesson,"},{"t":17.7,"txt":"instrumentation is measuring the real-life conditions of a plant's process. Let us take an"},{"t":23.2,"txt":"electronic pressure transmitter that is measuring the pressure inside a vessel. The instrument is"},{"t":29.2,"txt":"connected to the site's control system via a 4 to 20 milliamp current signal, the control system then"},{"t":35.3,"txt":"gives a readout to our control room operator so we can monitor and know the exact state of the plant."},{"t":41.7,"txt":"But how does the control room operator know that the pressure he is seeing on his screen"},{"t":46.3,"txt":"is the exact pressure that is in the vessel?"},{"t":49.4,"txt":"What makes him trust that this instrumentation is accurate and reliable. In many process industries,"},{"t":55.9,"txt":"the precision of process variables instrumentation is measuring is extremely important."},{"t":61.4,"txt":"For quality of the product that is being created. The safety of people and equipment,"},{"t":66.1,"txt":"and for the profitability of the business. Regular calibration of the instrumentation is what gives"},{"t":71.9,"txt":"us this confidence. Calibration is the process of comparing plant instrumentation to a known"},{"t":77.8,"txt":"quantity to check for the instrumentation's accuracy. Adjustments are then made if the"},{"t":82.8,"txt":"accuracy of the equipment is out of its allowed tolerance. The known quantity instrumentation is"},{"t":88.2,"txt":"checked against is usually in the form of test equipment that is regularly calibrated to a high"},{"t":93.4,"txt":"degree of accuracy. Test equipment calibration is often carried out at dedicated calibration labs"},{"t":100,"txt":"that will be accredited to certain standards, depending on the country you're operating in."},{"t":104.7,"txt":"Here in the UK UKAS is an accreditation body that will ensure a calibration lab is certifying its"},{"t":110.7,"txt":"equipment to the appropriate standard. Let's look at how we would carry out a calibration using"},{"t":115.8,"txt":"our vessel pressure transmitter as an example. We are going to assume the transmitter has already"},{"t":121.5,"txt":"been removed and is in the workshop ready to be calibrated. Calibration is often performed in situ"},{"t":127.1,"txt":"but that's something we'll discuss in a follow-up video. We would first need to know the range of the"},{"t":131.9,"txt":"instrument so that we know what test equipment to select and to calculate our test points."},{"t":137.4,"txt":"The range might be printed on data labels on the instrument or we could look at the control system"},{"t":142.7,"txt":"block we are connected to in order to find the range. We would then connect a calibrated,"},{"t":147.8,"txt":"suitably ranged pressure pump or calibrator to our instrument via its process connection."},{"t":154.2,"txt":"We would also connect the transmitter electrically to a calibrator to test the 4 to 20 milliamp current"},{"t":159.6,"txt":"signal that the transmitter gives out to different inputs, this is what the control system is"},{"t":164.6,"txt":"converting to a reading for our process operator. We would then apply various test pressures"},{"t":170.2,"txt":"along the range of the transmitter and record the values on a calibration certificate. In a"},{"t":175.8,"txt":"five point calibration we will often be testing 0 25 50 75 and 100 % of the range of our transmitter."},{"t":185.4,"txt":"We would work out if the transmitter is within the required accuracy for specific piece of equipment,"},{"t":191,"txt":"something like one percent of range maximum error is usual for general purpose pressure transmitters."},{"t":197.2,"txt":"We would also check for zero span and hysteresis errors."},{"t":201.6,"txt":"this is called the \"as found\" test. If the pressure transmitter is out of its calibration limits"},{"t":208,"txt":"we would adjust the range or zero either through local potentiometers or buttons on the transmitter,"},{"t":214.6,"txt":"or more commonly on newer equipment digitally via a field device communicator"},{"t":219.8,"txt":"such as a HART. We would then repeat the test to ensure we have met our calibration standard,"},{"t":227,"txt":"this is called the \"as left\" test. The information we have obtained about the"},{"t":232,"txt":"accuracy of the transmitter will be used to create a calibration certificate usually electronically,"},{"t":237.7,"txt":"this will then likely be stored in the maintenance management system for future reference."},{"t":242.7,"txt":"The equipment is usually labelled as calibrated and dated and then returned to service."},{"t":249.7,"txt":"Before I discuss calibration frequency I'd like to ask what other information you would like to know about"},{"t":254.8,"txt":"calibration or other instrumentation topics down below in the comments now. Remember to subscribe"},{"t":260.8,"txt":"and you'll be able to see the videos I create in response to your queries. So what determines"},{"t":266,"txt":"how often we calibrate an instrument duty? If a transmitter's accuracy is safety and quality"},{"t":272.2,"txt":"critical it might be calibrated monthly. If it is just giving supplementary information it might be"},{"t":278.2,"txt":"only calibrated every two years. Manufacturer guidance - It can also be dependent on the"},{"t":283.4,"txt":"transmitter type and the manufacturer will provide a recommended calibration period in its literature."},{"t":289.7,"txt":"Standards - if as part of your manufacturing process you are credited to ISO or other standards"},{"t":296.2,"txt":"then equipment calibration frequency is highly controlled and it will determine the frequency."},{"t":302.8,"txt":"Failure - Transmitters may need to be replaced and new equipment should be calibrated before being"},{"t":309,"txt":"put into service. Events - Sometimes process operators may suspect equipment to be out"},{"t":315.4,"txt":"of calibration due to abnormal readings, investigatory calibration may be required"},{"t":321.4,"txt":"to restore confidence in the equipment. I will be following up this video with a walkthrough example"},{"t":327.1,"txt":"in calculating max error and filling in calibration certificate as well as calibration"},{"t":333,"txt":"error types. If you have enjoyed the video and found it helpful then please like and subscribe."}],"words":[{"t":0.16,"w":"I'm"},{"t":0.16,"w":"going"},{"t":0.16,"w":"to"},{"t":0.16,"w":"explain"},{"t":0.16,"w":"all"},{"t":0.16,"w":"about"},{"t":0.16,"w":"instrumentation"},{"t":0.16,"w":"calibration"},{"t":0.16,"w":"and"},{"t":0.16,"w":"why"},{"t":0.16,"w":"is"},{"t":0.16,"w":"so"},{"t":0.16,"w":"vital"},{"t":0.16,"w":"in"},{"t":0.16,"w":"industry."},{"t":6.08,"w":"Let"},{"t":6.08,"w":"us"},{"t":6.08,"w":"start"},{"t":6.08,"w":"with"},{"t":6.08,"w":"an"},{"t":6.08,"w":"overview"},{"t":6.08,"w":"of"},{"t":6.08,"w":"what"},{"t":6.08,"w":"calibration"},{"t":6.08,"w":"is"},{"t":6.08,"w":"and"},{"t":6.08,"w":"why"},{"t":6.08,"w":"it"},{"t":6.08,"w":"is"},{"t":6.08,"w":"needed,"},{"t":6.08,"w":"I"},{"t":6.08,"w":"will"},{"t":6.08,"w":"then"},{"t":6.08,"w":"discuss"},{"t":6.08,"w":"the"},{"t":11.44,"w":"calibration"},{"t":11.44,"w":"process"},{"t":11.44,"w":"and"},{"t":11.44,"w":"talk"},{"t":11.44,"w":"about"},{"t":11.44,"w":"calibration"},{"t":11.44,"w":"frequency."},{"t":11.44,"w":"As"},{"t":11.44,"w":"we"},{"t":11.44,"w":"learnt"},{"t":11.44,"w":"in"},{"t":11.44,"w":"the"},{"t":11.44,"w":"transmitter"},{"t":11.44,"w":"lesson,"},{"t":17.68,"w":"instrumentation"},{"t":17.68,"w":"is"},{"t":17.68,"w":"measuring"},{"t":17.68,"w":"the"},{"t":17.6